<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Medieval Overhaul compat for arachne silk (user's call 2026-09-26: "an arachne spun out our silk
		instead of MO's silk, even with MO installed"). Everything here is gated on MO being loaded;
		without MO the game is untouched and she spins `PMM_ArachneSilk`.

		1. What she spins. Being a `Fabric`/`Textiles` textile is not enough for MO: MO's silk rugs and
		   royal furniture take their silk as a *named* ingredient - `<DankPyon_Silk>150</DankPyon_Silk>`
		   in a costList - and no fabric category substitutes for that. So with MO loaded the race's
		   `CompProperties_ArachneSilk/silkDef` is re-pointed from `PMM_ArachneSilk` to
		   `DankPyon_Silk`, and a colony running MO has one silk rather than two.

		   Op 1 removes the existing element and op 2 adds the new one, rather than one
		   `PatchOperationReplace`: `PatchOperationAdd` appends the children of `<value>` (verified in
		   `XmlContainer.LoadDataFromXmlCustom`, where `node = xmlRoot`), which is unambiguous, and the
		   two ops always match because the element they touch ships in our own race def. Order matters
		   - op 2's xpath needs the element to be gone, so op 2 matches the comp without any `silkDef`.

		2. Our own def must not appear from nowhere. With MO loaded nothing produces `PMM_ArachneSilk`
		   any more, so it is added to the `excludedThingDefs` of every trader generator that stocks the
		   `Textiles` category. `StockGenerator_Category.GenerateThings` builds stock from
		   `categoryDef.DescendantThingDefs.Where(t => t.tradeability.TraderCanSell() && ...)` and that
		   per-generator list is the only per-item escape hatch; nothing in this load order stocks
		   textiles by tag (`<tag>Textiles</tag>` appears nowhere).

		   Deliberately NOT touched: `tradeability`. `None` would keep the silk off a trader's shelves
		   but also stop the player selling it. `excludedThingDefs` stops only the *generation* of
		   trader stock, so a spare bundle can still be sold.

		   51 `StockGenerator_Category` generators stock `Textiles` in this load order and 11 of them
		   (Core's outlander, neolithic, caravan and orbital kinds, Royalty's empire, plus Keshig and
		   Forsaken) already carry an `excludedThingDefs` element. Op 3 appends into those existing
		   elements; op 4 adds the element to the generators that lack one. Reversing those two would
		   let op 4 match the generators op 3 had just changed and write the defName in twice.

		   Gated on MO by display name: `PatchOperationFindMod` compares with
		   `ModLister.HasActiveModWithName`, an exact `ModMetaData.Name` test, not a packageId test.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Medieval Overhaul</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
			<operations>
				<li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PMM_Race_Arachne"]/comps/li/silkDef</xpath>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PMM_Race_Arachne"]/comps/li[@Class="PMM_Insects.CompProperties_ArachneSilk"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<silkDef>DankPyon_Silk</silkDef>
					</value>
				</li>
				<!-- The ant mimic (2026-09-27) spins the same silk, so her race needs the
				     same two ops. Written out rather than looped over both defNames: a
				     PatchOperation names one def per xpath, and two explicit pairs are
				     easier to read than a "PMM_Race_A (or B)" predicate. -->
				<li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PMM_Race_AntArachne"]/comps/li/silkDef</xpath>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="PMM_Race_AntArachne"]/comps/li[@Class="PMM_Insects.CompProperties_ArachneSilk"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<silkDef>DankPyon_Silk</silkDef>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/*[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][normalize-space(categoryDef)="Textiles"]/excludedThingDefs</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>PMM_ArachneSilk</li>
					</value>
				</li>
				<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef/stockGenerators/*[@Class="StockGenerator_Category"][normalize-space(categoryDef)="Textiles"][not(excludedThingDefs)]</xpath>
					<value>
						<excludedThingDefs>
							<li>PMM_ArachneSilk</li>
						</excludedThingDefs>
					</value>
				</li>
			</operations>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
